@inproceedings{WOS:001585275100029,
  abstract = {A reliable and transparent prediction model for hospital readmission is
essential to decrease unexpected costs and improve patient's health.
This research proposes a novel comprehensive approach that leverages a
generative AI mechanism to extract Frailty Index (FI) features for
predicting hospital readmission by utilizing diverse data types. Our
approach calculates FI using both structured data and detailed clinical
notes, ensuring a more accurate reflection of clinical assessments, and
addressing the limitations of existing models regarding both
explainability and data diversity. The proposed approach provides an
explainable framework that aligns with real-life clinical
decision-making processes, identifying key factors contributing to
readmission risk. It has significant implications for healthcare
professionals, researchers, and policymakers, with the potential to
improve patient outcomes, reduce healthcare costs, and enhance the
overall quality of care. Our findings demonstrate the value of
generative AI and the use of FI in providing transparent and accurate
predictions, offering valuable explanations and reasoning behind
predictive modeling.},
